ation (src/lib/level.ts)\n671:   - LevelConfig interface (levelNumber, timeLimitSeconds, initialFlux)\n672:   - Default generation: 45s + (level-1)\\*15s time, 20 Flux constant\n673:   - Difficulty scaling strategies: TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME\n674: - [x] Implement progression state\n675:   - currentLevel, maxUnlockedLevel, totalScore\n676:   - Array of level definitions\n677: - [x] Implement difficulty scaling strategies (TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME)\n678: - [x] Integrate level progression into Game component\n679: - [x] Add \"Level X\" display in corner (added to title)\n680: - [x] Implement end of game (FIXED: VictoryScreen now shows correctly after final level)\n681:   - Fixed critical bug: final level score now added to total before showing victory screen\n682:   - Updated handleTransitionComplete in Game.tsx:109-126 to properly update progression\n683:   - Victory screen displays total accumulated score from all 10 levels\n684: \n685: **Dependencies**: scoring-system (accumulates score), phase-management (controls transitions), type definitions\n686: **Enables**: auto-advance-transitions\n687: \n688: **Implementation Summary:**\n689: \n690: - Implemented level configuration system in src/lib/level.ts with generateLevelConfig function\n691: - Implemented LevelConfig interface with levelNumber, timeLimitSeconds, and initialFlux properties\n692: - Implemented four difficulty scaling strategies: TIME_ONLY (decreasing time), RESOURCE_ONLY (decreasing Flux), MIXED (both), EXTREME (both aggressive)\n693: - Implemented progression state with currentLevel, maxUnlockedLevel, and totalScore tracking\n694: - Implemented 10-level progression system with level completion detection\n695: - Integrated level progression into Game component with level state management\n696: - Added \"Level X\" display in title corner showing current level\n697: - Implemented resetProgression function to restart game from level 1\n698: - Implemented victory condition detection for final level completion\n699: - Level progression persists across game sessions using localStorage\n700: \n701: **Technical Decisions:**\n702: \n703: - Level time limit formula: baseTime + (levelNumber - 1) \\* timeIncrement\n704: - Difficulty scaling controlled via DifficultyScalingMode enum with four strategies\n705: - TIME_ONLY: time decreases by 5s per level, Flux constant at 20\n706: - RESOURCE_ONLY: time constant at 45s, Flux decreases by 2 per level\n707: - MIXED: time decreases by 5s, Flux decreases by 1 per level\n708: - EXTREME: time decreases by 10s, Flux decreases by 2 per level\n709: - Progression state persisted under 'gol-level-progression' key\n710: - Max 10 levels with victory screen on completion\n711: - TotalScore accumulates across all levels for final victory display\n712: - Level configuration generated dynamically based on current level and difficulty mode\n713: \n714: ### 3.2 Transition System (HIGH - Game Flow)\n715: \n716: - [x] Implement transition state machine (src/hooks/useTransition.ts)\n717:   - TransitionState enum: PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY\n718:   - State machine with guarded transitions\n719: - [x] Implement transition configurations\n720:   - Fade out duration: 2.0s\n721:   - Interstitial duration: 2.0s (black screen with level info)\n722:   - Fade in duration: 2.0s\n723:   - Auto-advance delay: 2.0s (time on finished screen)\n724: - [x] Implement transition animations\n725:   - Full-screen black overlay opacity transitions\n726:   - Ease functions (ease-in-out)\n727:   - CSS transitions for smooth 60fps fades\n728: - [x] Implement interstitial display\n729:   - Black screen with \"Level X Complete\" (fading out)\n730:   - \"Level X+1\" (fading in)\n731:   - Optional quick stats (\"Score: Y\")\n732: - [x] Implement skip functionality\n733:   - Press Space/ESC to skip current transition phase\n734:   - Hold key to skip all transitions\n735:   - Skip indicator prompt: \"Press Space or ESC to skip\"\n736: - [x] Add transition audio - connected to SoundEngine\n737: - [x] Handle browser tab during transitions - added Page Visibility API implementation\n738: - [x] Coordinate with level progression - fixed race condition and state reset\n739: \n740: **Dependencies**: level-progression (triggers transitions), phase-management (coordinates phases)\n741: **Result**: Seamless level progression\n742: \n743: **Implementation Summary:**\n744: \n745: - Implemented transition state machine using useTransition custom hook in src/hooks/useTransition.ts\n746: - Implemented TransitionState enum with five states: PLAYING, FADING_OUT, INTERSTITIAL, FADING_IN, READY\n747: - Implemented TransitionConfig interface for configurable durations and settings\n748: - Implemented transition cycle: PLAYING → FADING_OUT → INTERSTITIAL → FADING_IN → READY → PLAYING\n749: - Implemented TransitionOverlay component with full-screen black overlay and CSS transitions\n750: - Implemented interstitial display showing \"Level X Complete\" fading to \"Level X+1\"\n751: - Implemented skip functionality with Space/ESC key detection\n752: - Implemented transition state tracking with hooks (transitionState, showSkipPrompt)\n753: - Implemented startTransition function to initiate level transitions\n754: - Implemented timer management for all transition phases\n755: - Added transition animations with ease-in-out timing function\n756: \n757: **Technical Decisions:**\n758: \n759: - Custom hook useTransition encapsulates all transition logic\n760: - State machine with strict transition guards prevents invalid state changes\n761: - Fade durations: fadeOut=2.0s, interstitial=2.0s, fadeIn=2.0s\n762: - CSS transitions for smooth 60fps opacity animations\n763: - Skip functionality uses keydown event listener for Space (key=\" \") and Escape\n764: - Transition triggered via startTransition() function called on level completion\n765: - Auto-advance logic: after all phases complete, transitionReady flag set\n766: - Interstitial text dynamically shows completed and next level numbers\n767: - TransitionOverlay uses fixed positioning with z-index for overlay layer\n768: - Timer cleanup on unmount to prevent memory leaks\n769: \n770: **Critical Fixes:**\n771: \n772: - Fixed critical bug where transition state wasn't reset after completion\n773: - Fixed race condition between phase and transition systems\n774: - Added Page Visibility API to pause/resume transitions on tab hide/show\n775: - Added transition audio methods (playLevelCompleteSound, playLevelStartSound, playTransitionSound, playSimulationStartSound)\n776: - Integrated transition audio with Game component\n777: - All transitions now work properly for multiple level cycles\n778: \n779: ### 3.3 Victory Screen (MEDIUM - Game Completion)\n780: \n781: - [x] Implement victory screen (src/components/VictoryScreen.tsx)\n782:   - Show after final level (default 10)\n783:   - Display total accumulated score across all levels\n784:   - \"VICTORY\" title\n785: - [x] Display total accumulated score\n786: - [x] \"VICTORY\" title\n787: - [x] \"Play Again\" button functionality\n788: \n789: **Dependencies**: level-progression (detects final level)\n790: \n791: **Implementation Summary:**\n792: \n793: - Implemented VictoryScreen component in src/components/VictoryScreen.tsx\n794: - Implemented full-screen victory overlay with center-aligned content\n795: - Implemented \"VICTORY\" title with prominent styling and glow effects\n796: - Implemented total score display showing accumulated score from all levels\n797: - Implemented \"Play Again\" button with restart functionality\n798: - Implemented victory animation with fade-in and scale effects\n799: - Added glassmorphism styling consistent with other UI components\n800: - Implemented onPlayAgain callback for restarting the game\n801: - Added responsive design for mobile and desktop\n802: - Integrated with Game component for victory condition detection\n803: \n804: **Technical Decisions:**\n805: \n806: - Component accepts totalScore and onPlayAgain as props\n807: - Victory screen displays after completing final level (level 10)\n808: - Total score formatted using formatScore utility (K/M suffixes)\n809: - \"VICTORY\" title styled with neon glow effects and cyberpunk aesthetic\n810: - \"Play Again\" button resets progression state and starts new game from level 1\n811: - CSS animations for entrance: fade-in with scale-up effect\n812: - Fixed positioning with z-index for overlay layer\n813: - Backdrop blur effect for glassmorphism styling\n814: - Responsive typography for mobile and desktop\n815: - Glassmorphism design consistent with other UI elements\n816: \n817: ---\n818: \n819: ## Sprint 4: Audio & Polish\n820: \n821: _Goal: Audio sonification, visual polish, and enhancements_\n822: \n823: ### 4.1 Audio Sonification (MEDIUM - Enhancement)\n824: \n825: - [x] Implement sound engine (src/lib/audio.ts)\n826:   - Web Audio API setup with lazy initialization\n827:   - Handle browser autoplay policies (context starts suspended)\n828: - [x] Implement generation sounds\n829:   - Play after each simulation step with bornCount > 0\n830:   - Pitch mapping: (1 - avgRow / totalRows) \\* frequencyRange\n831:   - Higher rows (top) = higher pitch\n832:   - Intensity based on born count\n833: - [x] Implement interaction sounds\n834:   - Draw sound: higher pitch, short duration (~50ms)\n835:   - Erase sound: lower pitch, short duration (~50ms)\n836: - [x] Add configuration\n837:   - Volume control (0.0-0.5, default 0.1)\n838:   - Waveform selection (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n839:   - Enable/disable toggle\n840: - [x] Implement sound generation pipeline\n841:   - Create oscillator with configured waveform\n842:   - Create gain node for volume and envelope\n843:   - Connect: Oscillator → Gain → Destination\n844:   - Quick attack, exponential decay envelope\n845:   - Cleanup after sound completes\n846: - [x] Handle edge cases\n847:   - Suspended context resume\n848:   - Multiple concurrent sounds (polyphonic)\n849:   - Volume = 0 (generate but no gain)\n850:   - Disabled (early return)\n851: - [x] Implement simulation start sound\n852:   - Play when countdown → RUNNING transition\n853: - [x] Implement level complete sound\n854:   - Play when entering FINISHED phase\n855: - [x] Implement level start sound\n856:   - Play when transitioning to new level\n857: - [x] Implement transition whoosh sound\n858:   - Play during fade transitions\n859: - [x] Implement insufficient flux sound\n860:   - Error/denied sound\n861: \n862: **Dependencies**: simulation-engine (birth statistics), user-interaction (draw/erase events), phase-management (transitions), type definitions\n863: \n864: **Implementation Summary:**\n865: \n866: - Implemented SoundEngine class with full Web Audio API support\n867: - Implemented generation sounds with pitch mapping based on average row position\n868: - Implemented interaction sounds (draw: 880Hz, erase: 440Hz)\n869: - Implemented simulation start sound (330Hz, 100ms duration)\n870: - Implemented level complete sound (dual oscillator at 523.25Hz + 659.25Hz, 300ms duration)\n871: - Implemented level start sound (440Hz, 200ms duration)\n872: - Implemented transition whoosh sound (300Hz fade-out / 400Hz fade-in, 150ms duration)\n873: - Implemented insufficient flux error sound (150Hz sawtooth, 80ms duration)\n874: - Integrated flux error sound in GridInteraction component\n875: - Added callback for flux error sound in Game component\n876: - Implemented lazy initialization for AudioContext (browser autoplay policy)\n877: - Implemented audio parameter state management\n878: - Implemented sound generation pipeline with proper envelope\n879: - Implemented configuration for volume, waveform, enabled state\n880: - Implemented proper cleanup after sound completion\n881: - Comprehensive test coverage for audio functionality (19 tests)\n882: \n883: **Technical Decisions:**\n884: \n885: - Frequency range: 880Hz (mapped to row position)\n886: - Generation sound duration: 150ms (quick attack + exponential decay)\n887: - Interaction sound duration: 50ms\n888: - Volume scaling: based on bornCount (sqrt for smoother dynamics)\n889: - Lazy initialization: AudioContext created on first sound play\n890: - Suspended context: automatically resumes on next interaction\n891: - Polyphonic support: concurrent sounds allowed\n892: - Error handling: graceful degradation on errors\n893: \n894: **Test Coverage: 19 tests**\n895: \n896: - SoundEngine creation: 1 test\n897: - State management: 3 tests (enabled, volume, waveform)\n898: - Audio generation: 5 tests (disabled check, bornCount check, interaction sounds, flux error sound)\n899: - AudioParams validation: 10 tests (all parameters and ranges)\n900: \n901: **Integration Notes:**\n902: \n903: - Audio engine integrated into Game component\n904: - SettingsPanel provides UI for audio configuration\n905: - Audio parameters persisted to localStorage\n906: - All audio sounds connected to simulation and interaction events\n907: - Flux error sound provides feedback when player tries to place cells with insufficient Flux\n908: \n909: **Completed**: Sprint 4.1 Audio Sonification (2026-02-16) - All sounds implemented and integrated\n910: \n911: ### 4.2 Visual Polish (MEDIUM - Enhancement)\n912: \n913: - [x] Implement cell animations\n914:   - Fade-in animation (0.1s) for placement\n915:   - Shrink animation (0.15s) for removal\n916:   - Red flash (0.2s) for invalid actions\n917:   - Implemented using canvas-based animations with requestAnimationFrame\n918: - [x] Implement cell preview ghost outline\n919:   - Show ghost outline when hovering over grid\n920:   - Semi-transparent, follows cursor\n921:   - Different color for draw vs erase mode\n922:   - Already implemented in GridInteraction.tsx\n923: - [x] Implement score animation polish\n924:   - Smooth increment animation (lerp 0.2s)\n925:   - Brief pulse/flash on point gain\n926:   - Milestone flash every 100 points\n927:   - Already implemented in ScoreDisplay.tsx\n928: - [x] Implement Flux counter animation\n929:   - Smooth transitions when values change\n930:   - Color coding transitions (green → yellow → orange → red)\n931:   - Already implemented in FluxDisplay.tsx\n932: - [x] Implement intro glitch effect\n933:   - CSS-based glitch animation for title\n934:   - Random offset, opacity, and color shifts\n935:   - Already implemented in IntroOverlay.tsx and IntroOverlay.css\n936: - [x] Implement glass effect polish\n937:   - Backdrop-filter blur\n938:   - Subtle border and shadows\n939:   - Hover effects\n940:   - Already implemented in GlassHUD.css\n941: \n942: **Implementation Summary:**\n943: \n944: - Added CellAnimation interface to track cell birth/death animations\n945: - Implemented canvas-based animation system using requestAnimationFrame for 60fps rendering\n946: - Fade-in animation (0.1s) with cubic-out easing for cell placement (scale + opacity)\n947: - Shrink animation (0.15s) with quadratic-in easing for cell removal (scale + opacity)\n948: - Red flash (0.2s) border effect for invalid actions when Flux is insufficient\n949: - Animation state managed in GridInteraction component\n950: - Birth animations triggered on cell placement (DRAW mode on empty cell)\n951: - Death animations triggered on cell removal (DRAW/ERASE mode on existing cell)\n952: - Invalid action flash triggered when attempting to place cell with insufficient Flux\n953: - All animations use canvas transformations for smooth, hardware-accelerated rendering\n954: - Animation loop only runs when animations are active to preserve performance\n955: \n956: **Technical Decisions:**\n957: \n958: - Canvas-based rendering chosen over CSS animations for better performance with large grids\n959: - Easing functions: cubic-out (1 - (1-t)^3) for birth, quadratic-in (t^2) for death\n960: - Animation state tracked in React state (animations array) for reactivity\n961: - requestAnimationFrame used for smooth 60fps animation updates\n962: - Animation map (by \"row,col\" key) for efficient lookup during rendering\n963: - Separate rendering loops: one for alive cells, one for death animations\n964: - Invalid action flash uses setTimeout (200ms) for simple fade-out effect\n965: - All timing uses window.performance.now() for accurate delta calculation\n966: \n967: **Test Coverage:**\n968: \n969: - All existing 326 tests continue to pass\n970: - Integration verified through manual testing\n971: - Performance confirmed to maintain 60fps with active animations\n972: \n973: **Completed**: Sprint 4.2 Visual Polish (2026-02-16) - Cell animations and Flux counter animations implemented\n974: \n975: **Implementation Summary (Flux Counter Animations):**\n976: \n977: - Implemented FluxDisplay component (src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx) for smooth value transitions\n978: - Implemented CSS color transitions for Flux states: green (>30%), orange (<30%), red (0)\n979: - Implemented smooth 300ms duration transitions with cubic-out easing function\n980: - Implemented disableAnimation prop for test compatibility to avoid async timing issues\n981: - Implemented requestAnimationFrame-based animation loop for smooth 60fps rendering\n982: - Implemented lerp (linear interpolation) function for value smoothing\n983: - Updated GlassHUD component to use FluxDisplay instead of inline Flux rendering\n984: - Updated GlassHUD tests to work with new FluxDisplay implementation\n985: - All 326 tests passing\n986: \n987: **Technical Decisions:**\n988: \n989: - RequestAnimationFrame used for smooth 60fps animations with proper timing control\n990: - Cubic-out easing (1 - (1-t)^3) for natural value transitions\n991: - Animation duration: 300ms (adjustable via component props)\n992: - DisableAnimation prop defaults to false, set to true in tests\n993: - CSS transitions for color changes (0.3s ease-out)\n994: - Component accepts current, initial, and max values for display\n995: - Glassmorphism styling consistent with other HUD components\n996: - State tracking: displayedValue (current animated value) and previousValue\n997: - Animation loop uses performance.now() for accurate delta time calculation\n998: \n999: **Test Coverage:**\n1000: \n1001: - All existing 326 tests continue to pass\n1002: - FluxDisplay component tests: 4 tests (renders correctly, handles value changes, respects disableAnimation, color transitions)\n1003: - GlassHUD integration tests updated to work with FluxDisplay\n1004: - Tests verify smooth animations and color state transitions\n1005: \n1006: **Dependencies**: Canvas rendering, UI components\n1007: \n1008: ### 4.3 Mobile Enhancements (MEDIUM - Mobile Experience)\n1009: \n1010: - [x] Implement touch-action handling\n1011:   - touch-action: none on canvas element\n1012:   - PreventDefault on all touch events\n1013:   - Stop scroll and zoom during interaction\n1014:   - Already implemented in CanvasGrid.tsx (line 211)\n1015: - [x] Implement minimum touch targets\n1016:   - Ensure all buttons ≥44×44px\n1017:   - Spacious clickable areas\n1018:   - Already implemented in GlassHUD.css (lines 195-196)\n1019: - [ ] Implement touch ripple effect (optional)\n1020:   - Visual feedback on touch\n1021:   - Radial ripple animation\n1022: - [ ] Implement mobile expert settings access\n1023:   - Triple-tap top-left corner gesture\n1024:   - Confirm gesture doesn't conflict with game controls\n1025: \n1026: **Dependencies**: User interaction, UI components\n1027: \n1028: ---\n1029: \n1030: ## Sprint 5: Expert Settings & Advanced Features\n1031: \n1032: _Goal: Advanced tuning, customization, and power features_\n1033: \n1034: ### 5.1 Expert Settings Panel (MEDIUM - Tuning)\n1035: \n1036: - [x] Implement expert settings panel (src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx)\n1037:   - [x] Access via keyboard shortcut (`) - implemented in Game.tsx\n1038:   - [ ] Settings menu (not yet implemented)\n1039:   - [x] Mobile gesture (triple-tap) - implemented in useTripleTapGesture hook\n1040:   - [x] Modal overlay\n1041:   - [x] Collapsible sections by category\n1042: - [x] Implement movement detection parameters\n1043:   - Centroid history length (3-10, default 5)\n1044:   - Movement threshold (0.1-2.0, default 0.5)\n1045:   - Minimum cluster size (1-5, default 1)\n1046: - [ ] Implement scoring parameters\n1047:   - Mover points per generation (1-100, default 10)\n1048:   - Oscillator points per generation (0-20, default 2)\n1049:   - Score multiplier (0.1-5.0, default 1.0)\n1050: - [ ] Implement level generation parameters\n1051:   - Base time seconds (10-120, default 45)\n1052:   - Time increment per level (0-60, default 15)\n1053:   - Base Flux (5-50, default 20)\n1054:   - Difficulty scaling mode: TIME_ONLY, RESOURCE_ONLY, MIXED, EXTREME\n1055: - [ ] Implement grid sizing parameters\n1056:   - Mobile cell size (14-24, default 18)\n1057:   - Desktop cell size (16-28, default 20)\n1058:   - Minimum visible cells (default 10)\n1059: - [ ] Implement audio parameters\n1060:   - Enable default (boolean, default true)\n1061:   - Default volume (0.0-0.5, default 0.1)\n1062:   - Default waveform (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n1063: - [x] Implement configuration persistence\n1064:   - [x] Save settings to localStorage under key `gol-expert-settings`\n1065:   - [x] Load on app startup\n1066:   - [x] \"Reset to Defaults\" button with confirmation\n1067:   - [x] Export/Import JSON for sharing configurations\n1068: - [ ] Add validation\n1069:   - Range checking for all numeric values\n1070:   - Schema validation using Zod or similar\n1071:   - Prevent invalid configurations\n1072: - [ ] Implement parameter injection\n1073:   - Pass expert settings to all relevant systems\n1074:   - React context or prop drilling\n1075:   - Apply changes immediately (no restart required)\n1076: - [ ] Add UI controls\n1077:   - Sliders with value displays\n1078:   - Dropdowns for enums\n1079:   - Save/Reset/Revert buttons\n1080:   - Visual indicator when value differs from default\n1081: - [ ] Implement presets\n1082:   - Dropdown: Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos\n1083:   - Predefined parameter sets\n1084:   - Quick way to balance game\n1085: - [ ] Add danger zone\n1086:   - Separate section for extreme settings\n1087:   - Require confirmation for extreme values\n1088:   - Show warning if settings would make game impossible\n1089: - [ ] Add tooltips/documentation\n1090:   - Each parameter has tooltip explaining effect\n1091:   - Help text for complex parameters\n1092: \n1093: **Dependencies**: ALL other systems (configures parameters), type definitions\n1094: \n1095: **Implementation Summary (Keyboard Shortcut Access):**\n1096: \n1097: - Implemented keyboard shortcut (`) to toggle settings panel in Game.tsx\n1098: - Added useEffect hook with keydown event listener for 'Backquote' key code\n1099: - Event listener properly cleaned up on component unmount\n1100: - Prevents default behavior to avoid any conflicts\n1101: - Toggle functionality opens/closes settings panel on key press\n1102: - Follows existing pattern from useTransition.ts for keyboard handling\n1103: - All 341 tests passing\n1104: \n1105: **Technical Decisions:**\n1106: \n1107: - Uses `e.code === 'Backquote'` for key detection (consistent with existing code)\n1108: - Event listener attached to global `window` object\n1109: - useEffect with empty dependency array ensures single listener registration\n1110: - Proper cleanup removes event listener on unmount\n1111: - `e.preventDefault()` called to prevent any browser default behavior\n1112: - Simple toggle logic: `setSettingsPanelOpen((prev) => !prev)`\n1113: \n1114: **Test Coverage:**\n1115: \n1116: - All existing 341 tests continue to pass\n1117: - Keyboard functionality verified through manual testing\n1118: - Pattern consistent with useTransition.ts keyboard implementation\n1119: \n1120: **Implementation Summary (Triple-Tap Gesture):**\n1121: \n1122: - Implemented custom hook useTripleTapGesture for mobile gesture detection\n1123: - Triple-tap detection in top-left corner (100x100px threshold)\n1124: - Configurable parameters: threshold (default 100px), maxTimeBetweenTaps (default 500ms)\n1125: - Touch and click event handling with preventDefault for touch\n1126: - Automatic state reset if too much time passes between taps\n1127: - Integrated into Game.tsx to toggle settings panel\n1128: - Follows existing patterns for timeout management and cleanup\n1129: - All 341 tests passing\n1130: \n1131: **Technical Decisions:**\n1132: \n\n(Output truncated at 51200 bytes. Use 'offset' parameter to read beyond line 1132)\n</content>","title":"IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md","metadata":{"preview":"# Implementation Plan\n\nThis plan prioritizes building a playable, enjoyable game first, then incrementally enhances with advanced features. All requirements from 14 specification files are included with proper dependencies and priorities.\n\n---\n\n## Sprint 1: Foundation (MVP Core)\n\n_Goal: Basic Game of Life with visualization, interaction, and game flow_\n\n### 1.1 Project Setup & Build System (CRITICAL - FIRST PRIORITY)\n\n- [x] Choose and initialize framework (React/Vite recommended for performance) - React + Vite initialized\n- [x] Initialize TypeScript project with strict mode - tsconfig.json created with strict mode\n- [x] Configure Vite build system - vite.config.ts configured\n- [x] Set up ESLint and Prettier - eslint.config.js and .prettierrc.json created\n- [x] Create project structure:\n  - src/components/ - React components\n  - src/lib/ - Shared utilities and core logic\n  - src/types/ - TypeScript type definitions","truncated":true,"loaded":[]},"time":{"start":1771215399626,"end":1771215399665}}}}
