{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771215494330,"sessionID":"ses_39b55e9f8fferWn8zBs1ZJmQ6V","part":{"id":"prt_c64aa48a7001HMoMWyEw7hpdhF","sessionID":"ses_39b55e9f8fferWn8zBs1ZJmQ6V","messageID":"msg_c64aa2bc1001W8MyAw63fusNcq","type":"tool","callID":"call_59e41b7948674944aa6650a6","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Study spec files deeply","prompt":"Study ALL files in specs/ directory. Read each specification file completely and understand:\n1. The full requirements and specifications\n2. All features and functionality described\n3. Technical requirements and constraints\n4. Implementation details\n5. Any dependencies between specifications\n\nReturn a comprehensive summary of all specifications, highlighting:\n- Core features and their requirements\n- Technical specifications (timeouts, durations, parameters, etc.)\n- Any implementation details mentioned\n- Dependencies between different specs\n- Priority or importance levels if mentioned\n\nBe thorough and read every spec file completely."},"output":"task_id: ses_39b55b824ffex9nZ90nDEG702d (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Specification Summary\n\nI've read and analyzed all 12 specification files in the `specs/` directory. Here's a comprehensive summary of the complete system:\n\n---\n\n## CORE SYSTEM ARCHITECTURE\n\n### 1. **Phase Management System** (phase-management.md)\n**Purpose**: State machine governing three core game phases\n\n**Phases**:\n- **PLANNING**: Unlimited time, place/remove cells using Flux\n- **RUNNING**: Fixed countdown timer (starts at 45s base), add-only cell placement\n- **FINISHED**: Brief pause (2.0s) before auto-advance\n\n**Technical Requirements**:\n- Phase transitions: PLANNING → COUNTDOWN (3,2,1) → RUNNING → FINISHED → PLANNING (next level)\n- START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- Simulation stops completely at level end (no carryover)\n- Must use accurate timing (Date.now() or performance.now())\n\n**Dependencies**: Integrated with flux-management, scoring-system, auto-advance-transitions\n\n---\n\n### 2. **Core Simulation Engine** (simulation-engine.md)\n**Purpose**: Computes cellular automaton generations using Conway's rules\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Age-based cell state (0=dead, >0=age in generations)\n- Toroidal boundary conditions (wrapping edges)\n- Moore neighborhood (8 adjacent cells)\n- Performance optimizations: Direct grid access via React ref, precomputed neighbor offsets\n\n**Data Structures**:\n```typescript\ntype GridType = number[][];\ninterface SimulationState {\n  grid: GridType;\n  generation: number;\n  running: boolean;\n  speed: number; // 10ms to 500ms\n}\n```\n\n**Dependencies**: Canvas rendering (grid state), Audio sonification (birth stats)\n\n---\n\n### 3. **Level Progression System** (level-progression.md)\n**Purpose**: Progressive difficulty through increasing time limits and limited Flux\n\n**Core Mechanics**:\n- **Time Limit**: Starts at 45s, increases by 15s per level (configurable)\n- **Initial Flux**: 20 per level (constant, configurable via expert settings)\n- **No Lose Condition**: Always advances to next level\n- **Score Accumulation**: Total score tracked across all levels\n\n**Difficulty Scaling Modes** (Expert Settings):\n- TIME_ONLY: Increase time, constant Flux\n- RESOURCE_ONLY: Constant time, decrease Flux\n- MIXED: Both adjusted\n- EXTREME: Aggressive Flux reduction\n\n**Transition Flow**:\n1. Level completes (timer=0 or all cells die)\n2. Fade out (2.0s)\n3. Loading/interstitial (2.0s)\n4. Fade in to next level (2.0s)\n5. Reset to PLANNING phase with fresh Flux\n\n**Dependencies**: auto-advance-transitions, phase-management, scoring-system\n\n---\n\n### 4. **Auto-Advance Transitions** (auto-advance-transitions.md)\n**Purpose**: Cinematic fade transitions between completed levels\n\n**Technical Parameters**:\n```typescript\ninterface TransitionConfig {\n  fadeOutDuration: 2.0s;\n  fadeInDuration: 2.0s;\n  interstitialDuration: 2.0s;\n  autoAdvanceDelay: 2.0s;\n  skipEnabled: true;\n}\n```\n\n**Transition States**: PLAYING → FADING_OUT → INTERSTITIAL → FADING_IN → READY\n\n**Key Features**:\n- Skip mechanism: Space/ESC skips to READY immediately\n- CSS transitions for smooth 60fps fades\n- Level complete/next level text displays\n- Audio transitions (chime, ambient, level start sound)\n- Browser tab handling: Pause transition timer when tab inactive\n\n**Edge Cases**:\n- Last level: Show victory screen with total accumulated score\n- Hold Space/ESC to skip all transitions rapidly\n\n**Dependencies**: level-progression (trigger source), phase-management\n\n---\n\n## RESOURCE & INTERACTION SYSTEMS\n\n### 5. **Flux Management** (flux-management.md)\n**Purpose**: Resource system limiting cell placement\n\n**Core Mechanics**:\n- **Initial Allocation**: 20 Flux per level (configurable: 5-50)\n- **Placement Cost**: 1 Flux per cell (both phases)\n- **Refund Mechanic**: Full refund during PLANNING phase only\n- **Play Phase**: Add-only, no refunds\n- **Strategic Choice**: Players decide Flux allocation between phases\n\n**State Structure**:\n```typescript\ninterface FluxState {\n  current: number;\n  initial: number;\n  placed: number;\n  removed: number;\n}\n```\n\n**UI Requirements**:\n- Color-coded display (Green/Yellow → Orange → Red)\n- Bar or counter showing current/initial\n- Audio feedback: Error sound, placement sound, removal sound\n- Smooth transitions on value changes\n\n**Dependencies**: phase-management, user-interaction\n\n---\n\n### 6. **User Interaction System** (user-interaction.md)\n**Purpose**: Mouse/touch input for drawing and erasing cells\n\n**Interaction Modes**: 'draw' | 'erase'\n\n**Event Handling**:\n- Mouse: down → move (while pressed) → up\n- Touch: start → move → end/cancel (prevent default for scrolling)\n- Coordinate conversion: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n\n**Mobile Considerations**:\n- `touch-action: none` on canvas\n- Responsive cell size (18px mobile, 20px desktop)\n- Minimum 44x44px touch targets\n- Prevent browser zoom/scroll\n\n**Dependencies**: Simulation engine (grid ref), Audio sonification (interaction sounds), Canvas rendering\n\n---\n\n### 7. **Grid Interaction** (grid-interaction.md)\n**Purpose**: Direct manipulation interface for cell placement\n\n**Core Features**:\n- Click to place/remove cells\n- START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- Interaction constraints: Disabled during RUNNING/FINISHED phases\n\n**UI States**:\n- Over empty cell (placeable): Crosshair or preview outline\n- Over empty cell (unplaceable): Forbidden symbol\n- Over live cell (removable): Minus icon or highlight\n\n**Visual Feedback**:\n- Cell preview follows cursor\n- Fade-in animation (0.1s) on placement\n- Shrink animation (0.15s) on removal\n- Red flash on invalid action\n\n---\n\n## SCORING & DETECTION SYSTEMS\n\n### 8. **Scoring System** (scoring-system.md)\n**Purpose**: Real-time score calculation based on cellular pattern classifications\n\n**Scoring Formula**:\n```typescript\ninterface ScoringConfig {\n  moverPointsPerGeneration: 10;  // Range: 1-100\n  oscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 2;  // Range: 0-20\n  staticPointsPerGeneration: 0;\n  scoreMultiplier: 1.0;  // Range: 0.1-5.0\n}\n```\n\n**Per-Generation Calculation**:\n- MOVER: 10 points × multiplier per generation\n- OSCILLATOR: 2 points × multiplier per generation\n- STATIC: 0 points\n- Score updates every generation during RUNNING phase\n\n**UI Requirements**:\n- Top-left display, large number with \"PTS\" label\n- Smooth increment animation (lerp 0.2s)\n- Brief pulse/flash on point gain\n- End-of-level stats: final score, time survived, patterns created\n\n**Persistence**:\n- Score resets to 0 each level (no carryover)\n- High score saved to localStorage per level\n\n**Dependencies**: movement-detection (cluster classifications)\n\n---\n\n### 9. **Movement Detection** (movement-detection.md)\n**Purpose**: Detect and classify cellular movement patterns via centroid tracking\n\n**Core Algorithm**:\n1. **Connected Component Detection**: 8-connectivity (diagonals included)\n2. **Centroid Tracking**: Track centroids across generations (default: 5 generations history)\n3. **Classification**:\n   - MOVER: Centroid translating (|dx| > 0.5 OR |dy| > 0.5)\n   - OSCILLATOR: Centroid static, cells changing locally\n   - STATIC: Both centroid and cells unchanged\n\n**Technical Parameters**:\n```typescript\ninterface TrackingConfig {\n  historyLength: 5;  // Generations to track (default)\n  movementThreshold: 0.5;  // Min distance to be moving\n}\n```\n\n**Performance Requirements**:\n- Must process in <16ms for 60fps\n- Optimize: Only recompute for changed regions\n- Scale with actual grid sizes (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n- Circular buffer for history storage\n\n**Edge Cases**:\n- Cluster split/merge (glider collisions)\n- Glider guns (gun is Static, gliders are Movers)\n- Minimum cluster size: 1 cell\n\n**Dependencies**: Scoring system (provides classifications)\n\n---\n\n## VISUAL & AUDIO SYSTEMS\n\n### 10. **Canvas Rendering System** (canvas-rendering.md)\n**Purpose**: High-performance grid rendering with age-based neon colors\n\n**Theme - Dark Neon**:\n- Background: `#0a0a0f`\n- Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (toggleable, only during PLANNING)\n\n**Age-Based Cell Colors**:\n- Age 0: `#00ffff` (cyan, 15px glow)\n- Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue, 8px glow)\n- Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta, 4px glow)\n- Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (purple, 2px glow)\n\n**Cell Size**:\n- Mobile (<768px): 18px\n- Desktop (≥768px): 20px\n- Updates on window resize\n\n**Rendering Pipeline**:\n1. Canvas resize with DPR scaling\n2. Transform reset\n3. Clear canvas\n4. Draw grid lines (if enabled)\n5. Draw live cells with age-based styling\n6. Update CSS variable `--life-intensity`\n\n**Performance Optimizations**:\n- `window.devicePixelRatio` for sharp rendering\n- Minimize context state changes\n- Optimize draws with useCallback\n\n**Dependencies**: Simulation engine (grid state), UI system (grid line toggle)\n\n---\n\n### 11. **Audio Sonification System** (audio-sonification.md)\n**Purpose**: Real-time sounds based on simulation and user interactions\n\n**Sound Engine Interface**:\n```typescript\ninterface SoundEngine {\n  setEnabled(enabled: boolean);\n  setVolume(volume: number);  // Range: 0.0-0.5\n  setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType);  // sine, triangle, square, sawtooth\n  playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number);\n  playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase');\n}\n```\n\n**Generation Sounds**:\n- Trigger: After each simulation step with bornCount > 0\n- Pitch: Based on average row position (higher row = higher pitch)\n- Formula: `pitch = (1 - avgRow / totalRows) * frequencyRange`\n- Volume: Scaled by bornCount\n\n**Interaction Sounds**:\n- Draw: Higher pitch (~880Hz), short (~50ms)\n- Erase: Lower pitch (~440Hz), short (~50ms)\n\n**Technical Details**:\n- Web Audio API with lazy initialization\n- AudioContext created on first user interaction (browser requirement)\n- Quick attack, exponential decay envelope\n- Concurrent sounds allowed (polyphonic)\n\n**Dependencies**: Simulation engine (birth statistics), User interaction (draw/erase triggers)\n\n---\n\n### 12. **UI/Overlay System** (ui-overlay.md)\n**Purpose**: Controls, configuration panels, and visual overlays\n\n**Key Components**:\n\n**Cinematic Intro Overlay**:\n- Shows on app load\n- \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n- CTA: \"ENTER VOID\" button\n- Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale\n\n**Glass HUD Container**:\n- Semi-transparent glass effect with blur\n- Floating overlay on bottom of screen\n- Main controls: PLAY/PAUSE, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR\n- Interaction modes: DRAW, ERASE\n- Status controls: Waveform selector, Volume slider (0-0.5, 0.01 step), Generation counter\n\n**Settings Panel**:\n- Speed slider (10ms to 500ms)\n- Grid size buttons: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n- Visuals checkbox: Show grid lines\n- Audio checkbox: Enable sonification\n- Expert settings access\n\n**Phase Status Display**:\n- Always visible\n- Shows: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n- Timer display (COUNTDOWN, RUNNING)\n- Flux counter (PLANNING, RUNNING)\n\n**CSS Architecture**:\n```css\n.glass-hud {\n  background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\n  backdrop-filter: blur(10px);\n  border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\n  border-radius: 12px;\n}\n```\n\n**Responsive Design**:\n- Desktop: Full width HUD centered at bottom\n- Mobile: Controls stack or scroll\n- Touch: Minimum 44px touch targets\n- Canvas: Adapts to window size\n\n**Dependencies**: All systems (configurable via settings panel)\n\n---\n\n### 13. **Expert Settings / Dev Panel** (expert-settings.md)\n**Purpose**: Hidden configuration interface for tuning game mechanics\n\n**Access Methods**:\n- Keyboard: Backtick (`) for quick access\n- Menu: Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\n- Mobile: Triple-tap top-left corner\n\n**Configurable Parameters**:\n\n**Movement Detection**:\n```typescript\ncentroidHistoryLength: 5;  // Range: 3-10\nmovementThreshold: 0.5;   // Range: 0.1-2.0\nminClusterSize: 1;         // Range: 1-5\n```\n\n**Scoring**:\n```typescript\nmoverPointsPerGeneration: 10;  // Range: 1-100\noscillatorPointsPerGeneration: 2;  // Range: 0-20\nscoreMultiplier: 1.0;  // Range: 0.1-5.0\n```\n\n**Level Generation**:\n```typescript\nbaseTimeSeconds: 45;  // Range: 10-120\ntimeIncrementPerLevel: 15;  // Range: 0-60\nbaseFlux: 20;  // Range: 5-50\ndifficultyScalingMode: 'TIME_ONLY' | 'RESOURCE_ONLY' | 'MIXED' | 'EXTREME';\n```\n\n**Grid Sizing**:\n```typescript\nmobileCellSize: 18;   // Range: 14-24\ndesktopCellSize: 20;  // Range: 16-28\nminVisibleCells: 10;\n```\n\n**Features**:\n- Real-time updates (no restart required)\n- Save to localStorage (`gol-expert-settings`)\n- Export/Import JSON\n- Reset to defaults\n- Visual indicator when value differs from default\n- \"Revert\" button per section\n- Danger zone with warnings for extreme values\n\n**Dependencies**: Affects all systems\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL DEPENDENCY GRAPH\n\n```\nExpert Settings (Global configuration)\n    ↓\n┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n│                   Phase Management                       │\n│  (orchestrates all systems through game phases)         │\n└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n    ↓\n    ├─→ Flux Management ←→ User Interaction System\n    │        ↓                    ↓\n    │   Grid Interaction   Canvas Rendering ← UI Overlay\n    │        ↓                    ↓\n    │    Scoring System ←→ Movement Detection\n    │        ↓\n    └─→ Level Progression ←→ Auto-Advance Transitions\n              ↓\n    ┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐\n    │              Core Simulation Engine                     │\n    │              (provides grid state)                     │\n    └─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘\n              ↓\n    Audio Sonification System (receives birth stats)\n```\n\n---\n\n## TECHNICAL SPECIFICATIONS SUMMARY\n\n### Time Durations\n- **Intro exit animation**: 1.2s\n- **Fade out**: 2.0s\n- **Interstitial**: 2.0s\n- **Fade in**: 2.0s\n- **Auto-advance delay**: 2.0s\n- **Cell placement animation**: 0.1s\n- **Cell removal animation**: 0.15s\n- **Score increment lerp**: 0.2s\n- **Countdown**: 3, 2, 1 (RUNNING starts after)\n- **Base level time**: 45s (increases by 15s per level)\n\n### Ranges & Limits\n- **Grid sizes**: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n- **Cell size**: Mobile 18px, Desktop 20px\n- **Simulation speed**: 10ms to 500ms between steps\n- **Audio volume**: 0.0 to 0.5 (default 0.1)\n- **Flux**: 5-50 (default 20)\n- **Score cap**: MAX_SAFE_INTEGER (9,007,199,254,740,991)\n- **Glow blur**: 2px to 15px based on age\n- **Touch targets**: Minimum 44px\n\n### Performance Requirements\n- **Movement detection**: <16ms for 60fps\n- **Large grid benchmark**: 100×100 grid, expect ~50-200 clusters max\n- **Canvas**: DPR scaling for sharp rendering\n- **Animation loop**: Use requestAnimationFrame with delta time check\n\n---\n\n## IMPLEMENTATION PRIORITY & CRITICAL PATH\n\n**Tier 1 - Core Foundation** (Must implement first):\n1. Core Simulation Engine\n2. Phase Management System\n3. Canvas Rendering System\n4. User Interaction System\n\n**Tier 2 - Game Mechanics** (Depend on Tier 1):\n5. Flux Management\n6. Scoring System\n7. Movement Detection\n8. Level Progression\n\n**Tier 3 - Polish & Enhancements** (Build on Tier 2):\n9. Audio Sonification System\n10. Auto-Advance Transitions\n11. UI/Overlay System (expert panel)\n\n**Tier 4 - Advanced Features**:\n12. Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n13. Cinematic Intro Overlay\n14. Grid Interaction refinements\n\n---\n\n## KEY TECHNICAL CONSTRAINTS\n\n1. **No Simulation Carryover**: Fresh start each level (grid, Flux, score all reset)\n2. **Audio Context**: Must be initialized on first user interaction (browser autoplay policy)\n3. **Touch Handling**: Prevent default on canvas to stop scrolling/zooming\n4. **Performance**: Movement detection must scale to grid sizes, use circular buffers\n5. **State Management**: Phase transitions must be guarded, no skipping\n6. **Browser Tab**: Timer continues running during gameplay, pauses during transitions\n7. **Mobile**: Minimum 44px touch targets, responsive cell sizes, prevent double-tap zoom\n8. **Accessibility**: Reduced motion preferences support for transitions\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive system describes a sophisticated Game of Life implementation with progression mechanics, resource management, pattern detection, and extensive audio-visual feedback. All specifications are well-documented with clear technical requirements, edge cases, and interdependencies.\n</task_result>","title":"Study spec files deeply","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b55b824ffex9nZ90nDEG702d","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771215407273,"end":1771215494327}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771215521171,"sessionID":"ses_39b55e9f8fferWn8zBs1ZJmQ6V","part":{"id":"prt_c64aa48aa001wxXx0CO2vjoR3P","sessionID":"ses_39b55e9f8fferWn8zBs1ZJmQ6V","messageID":"msg_c64aa2bc1001W8MyAw63fusNcq","type":"tool","callID":"call_24a5f5478ad149f5b9bd34d1","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Study source code structure","prompt":"Explore the src/ directory structure thoroughly. Identify:\n1. All files in src/ and its subdirectories\n2. The architecture and organization of the codebase\n3. What has been implemented vs what is missing\n4. Main components and their responsibilities\n5. Key utilities and libraries\n6. Current state of implementation\n\nRead key files to understand:\n- Components structure\n- State management approach\n- Integration patterns\n- Any TODOs or incomplete implementations\n\nReturn a detailed summary of the codebase structure and current implementation status."},"output":"task_id: ses_39b55b817ffe4xO5Z72BOIqlsR (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Detailed Codebase Structure and Implementation Status\n\n### 1. All Files in src/ Directory\n\nThe codebase contains **65 files** organized into the following structure:\n\n**Root Files:**\n- `/src/main.tsx` - Application entry point\n- `/src/App.tsx` - Main app component\n- `/src/App.test.tsx` - App tests\n- `/src/vite-env.d.ts` - Vite type definitions\n\n**Components (13 components):**\n- `/src/components/Game.tsx` - Main game controller component (479 lines)\n- `/src/components/CanvasGrid.tsx` - Canvas-based grid rendering (218 lines)\n- `/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx` - Grid interaction wrapper (230 lines)\n- `/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx` - Glass-morphism heads-up display (169 lines)\n- `/src/components/ScoreDisplay.tsx` - Score display with animations (130 lines)\n- `/src/components/SettingsPanel.tsx` - Expert settings panel (559 lines)\n- `/src/components/TransitionOverlay.tsx` - Level transition overlay (74 lines)\n- `/src/components/VictoryScreen.tsx` - Victory screen (58 lines)\n- `/src/components/IntroOverlay.tsx` - Intro screen (32 lines)\n- `/src/components/FluxDisplay.tsx` - Flux resource display (74 lines)\n- `/src/components/LevelStats.tsx` - Level statistics display (101 lines)\n- `/src/components/UIToggleButton.tsx` - UI visibility toggle (44 lines)\n\n**Custom Hooks (3 hooks):**\n- `/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts` - Game phase timer management (135 lines)\n- `/src/hooks/useTransition.ts` - Transition state management (191 lines)\n- `/src/hooks/useTripleTapGesture.ts` - Triple-tap gesture detection (88 lines)\n\n**Library/Utilities (13 modules):**\n- `/src/lib/simulation.ts` - Game of Life simulation logic (138 lines)\n- `/src/lib/state.ts` - State management utilities (114 lines)\n- `/src/lib/phase.ts` - Game phase state machine (166 lines)\n- `/src/lib/flux.ts` - Flux resource management (57 lines)\n- `/src/lib/movement.ts` - Pattern movement detection (254 lines)\n- `/src/lib/scoring.ts` - Scoring system (93 lines)\n- `/src/lib/level.ts` - Level progression system (164 lines)\n- `/src/lib/settings.ts` - Settings management (126 lines)\n- `/src/lib/audio.ts` - Audio/sound engine (270 lines)\n- `/src/lib/interaction.ts` - Grid interaction utilities (60 lines)\n- `/src/lib/validation.ts` - Input validation (56 lines)\n- `/src/lib/canvasUtils.ts` - Canvas rendering utilities (30 lines)\n- `/src/lib/logger.ts` - Logging utility (46 lines)\n\n**Types:**\n- `/src/types/index.ts` - TypeScript type definitions (110 lines)\n\n**Styles (8 CSS files):**\n- `/src/styles/index.css` - Global styles\n- `/src/styles/GlassHUD.css` - HUD styles (245 lines)\n- `/src/styles/ScoreDisplay.css` - Score display styles (166 lines)\n- `/src/styles/SettingsPanel.css` - Settings panel styles (311 lines)\n- `/src/styles/IntroOverlay.css` - Intro screen styles (160 lines)\n- `/src/styles/LevelStats.css` - Level stats styles (123 lines)\n- `/src/styles/FluxDisplay.css` - Flux display styles (16 lines)\n\n**Test Setup:**\n- `/src/test/setup.ts` - Test environment setup (29 lines)\n\n**Test Files (21 test files):**\nAll major library files and components have corresponding test files with good coverage\n\n---\n\n### 2. Architecture and Organization\n\n**Architecture Pattern:** Component-based with utility libraries, following a clean separation of concerns\n\n**Key Architectural Decisions:**\n\n1. **State Management:** Uses React hooks (useState, useReducer) with no external state library. The `Game.tsx` component acts as the main controller managing all game state.\n\n2. **Phase-Based Game Flow:** Implements a 4-phase game lifecycle:\n   - PLANNING: User places cells with limited flux resources\n   - COUNTDOWN: 3-second countdown before simulation starts\n   - RUNNING: Simulation runs with time limit\n   - FINISHED: Results display before transition\n\n3. **Custom Hooks Pattern:** Encapsulates complex logic:\n   - `usePhaseTimer`: Manages game phases with visibility change handling\n   - `useTransition`: Handles level transitions with tab visibility support\n   - `useTripleTapGesture`: Enables hidden settings access via gesture\n\n4. **Library Pattern:** Pure functional libraries separated by concern:\n   - Simulation logic\n   - Pattern detection/movement tracking\n   - Scoring system\n   - Level generation\n   - Audio engine\n   - Validation\n\n5. **Type Safety:** Comprehensive TypeScript types with strict mode enabled\n\n6. **Testing Strategy:** Unit tests for all library functions, component tests for UI\n\n---\n\n### 3. What Has Been Implemented vs What Is Missing\n\n**FULLY IMPLEMENTED:**\n\n1. **Core Simulation Engine**\n   - Conway's Game of Life rules\n   - Grid management with toroidal (wrapping) edges\n   - Grid size presets (Small/Medium/Large)\n   - Age tracking for cells\n\n2. **Pattern Detection System**\n   - Connected component clustering (BFS)\n   - Centroid tracking\n   - Velocity calculation\n   - Pattern classification (MOVER, OSCILLATOR, STATIC)\n\n3. **Resource Management**\n   - Flux system - limited cell placement\n   - Refund on cell removal (only in PLANNING phase)\n   - Color-coded flux indicators\n\n4. **Scoring System**\n   - Points for moving patterns (10 pts/generation default)\n   - Points for oscillating patterns (2 pts/generation default)\n   - Score multipliers\n   - High score tracking per level (localStorage)\n   - Score animations and milestone detection\n\n5. **Level Progression**\n   - 10 levels with configurable parameters\n   - Multiple difficulty scaling modes:\n     - TIME_ONLY: Time increases each level\n     - RESOURCE_ONLY: Flux decreases each level\n     - MIXED: Both time and flux adjust\n     - EXTREME: Both time and flux become harder\n   - Level transitions with statistics\n   - Victory screen on completion\n\n6. **UI Components**\n   - Canvas-based grid with performance optimizations\n   - Glass-morphism HUD\n   - Score display with animations\n   - Level statistics breakdown\n   - Settings panel with export/import\n   - Intro and transition overlays\n   - UI visibility toggle\n\n7. **Audio Engine**\n   - Web Audio API integration\n   - Generation sounds based on birth count and position\n   - Interaction sounds (draw/erase)\n   - Level complete/start sounds\n   - Transition sounds\n   - Configurable waveforms (sine, triangle, square, sawtooth)\n   - Volume control\n\n8. **Interaction System**\n   - Draw/Erase modes\n   - Hover highlighting\n   - Click and touch support\n   - Invalid action feedback\n   - Grid visibility toggle\n\n9. **Expert Settings**\n   - Movement detection parameters\n   - Scoring configuration\n   - Level generation parameters\n   - Grid sizing\n   - Audio configuration\n   - Export/Import settings as JSON\n\n10. **Testing Infrastructure**\n    - Comprehensive unit tests for all libraries\n    - Component tests\n    - Test setup with localStorage mocking\n    - Vitest configuration\n\n**MINOR GAPS / POTENTIAL IMPROVEMENTS:**\n\n1. **Missing CSS Files:**\n   - `VictoryScreen.css` is imported but file doesn't exist\n   - `TransitionOverlay.css` is imported but file doesn't exist\n   - These components use inline styles or may need CSS added\n\n2. **No Persistent Game Save:**\n   - Settings are saved to localStorage\n   - High scores are saved per level\n   - But no full game state persistence (e.g., resume where left off)\n\n3. **No Undo/Redo:**\n   - No way to undo cell placements during PLANNING phase\n\n4. **Limited Pattern Presets:**\n   - Only random fill option\n   - No famous patterns (glider, blinker, etc.) presets\n\n5. **No Pattern Library:**\n   - Players cannot save/load their own patterns\n\n6. **No Replay System:**\n   - No way to watch previous simulations\n\n7. **No Multiplayer:**\n   - Single-player only\n\n8. **No Tutorial:**\n   - Intro overlay is just a title screen\n   - No in-game instructions or tutorial\n\n**NO MAJOR MISSING FEATURES** - The core game is complete and polished!\n\n---\n\n### 4. Main Components and Their Responsibilities\n\n| Component | Lines | Responsibility |\n|-----------|-------|----------------|\n| **Game.tsx** | 479 | Main controller - manages all game state, coordinates systems, handles audio, level transitions, scoring, and UI orchestration |\n| **CanvasGrid.tsx** | 218 | Renders the grid using HTML5 Canvas with cell age-based colors, blur effects, animations, and high-DPI support |\n| **GridInteraction.tsx** | 230 | Wraps CanvasGrid with click/touch handling, flux management, cell placement/removal, and invalid action feedback |\n| **GlassHUD.tsx** | 169 | Displays all controls (START, STEP, RANDOM, CLEAR, grid size, draw/erase modes) and status information |\n| **ScoreDisplay.tsx** | 130 | Shows animated score, high score, and pattern breakdown (movers, oscillators, rate) |\n| **SettingsPanel.tsx** | 559 | Full settings UI with sliders/selects for all expert settings, export/import JSON, reset to defaults |\n| **TransitionOverlay.tsx** | 74 | Handles fade-out/interstitial/fade-in transitions between levels with statistics |\n| **VictoryScreen.tsx** | 58 | Displays total score and final level stats when all levels completed |\n| **IntroOverlay.tsx** | 32 | Simple title screen with glitch effect animation |\n| **FluxDisplay.tsx** | 74 | Animated flux counter with color coding (green/yellow/orange/red) |\n| **LevelStats.tsx** | 101 | Detailed statistics display (score, time, patterns, generations, cells) |\n| **UIToggleButton.tsx** | 44 | Eye icon button to show/hide the entire UI |\n\n---\n\n### 5. Key Utilities and Libraries\n\n**Simulation & Logic:**\n- `simulation.ts` - Core Game of Life engine (138 lines)\n- `movement.ts` - Pattern detection and tracking (254 lines)\n- `scoring.ts` - Score calculations (93 lines)\n- `phase.ts` - Game phase state machine (166 lines)\n\n**Game Systems:**\n- `level.ts` - Level generation and progression (164 lines)\n- `flux.ts` - Resource management (57 lines)\n- `audio.ts` - SoundEngine class with Web Audio API (270 lines)\n\n**Utilities:**\n- `state.ts` - Generic state management utilities (114 lines)\n- `validation.ts` - Input validation helpers (56 lines)\n- `interaction.ts` - Grid coordinate conversion (60 lines)\n- `canvasUtils.ts` - Canvas rendering helpers (30 lines)\n- `logger.ts` - Logging utility (46 lines)\n- `settings.ts` - Settings validation (126 lines)\n\n**Custom Hooks:**\n- `usePhaseTimer.ts` - Phase management with visibility handling (135 lines)\n- `useTransition.ts` - Transition orchestration (191 lines)\n- `useTripleTapGesture.ts` - Secret settings access gesture (88 lines)\n\n---\n\n### 6. Current State of Implementation\n\n**Status: PRODUCTION-READY**\n\nThe codebase is a **complete, fully-featured implementation** of Conway's Game of Life as a strategic puzzle game. Key observations:\n\n**Strengths:**\n1. ✅ **Comprehensive Testing** - Every library has corresponding test files\n2. ✅ **Type Safety** - Full TypeScript with strict mode enabled\n3. ✅ **Code Quality** - ESLint, Prettier configured, consistent style\n4. ✅ **Performance** - Canvas rendering with requestAnimationFrame, efficient algorithms\n5. ✅ **Accessibility** - ARIA labels, keyboard shortcuts (`G` for grid, backtick for settings)\n6. ✅ **Responsive Design** - Mobile-friendly with breakpoints and touch support\n7. ✅ **User Experience** - Smooth animations, glass-morphism UI, sound feedback\n8. ✅ **Expert Features** - Extensive customization via settings panel\n9. ✅ **Progression System** - 10 levels with multiple difficulty modes\n10. ✅ **Pattern Recognition** - Sophisticated movement detection algorithm\n\n**Code Organization:**\n- Clean separation of concerns (components vs libraries)\n- Functional programming patterns in libraries\n- React hooks for state management\n- No external state management dependencies\n\n**No TODOs or incomplete implementations found** - only test comments referencing debug log format\n\n**Dependencies:**\n- **Minimal dependencies:** Only React 19.2.4 and React-DOM 19.2.4\n- **No external UI libraries** - All custom components\n- **No state management libraries** - Uses React hooks\n- **Testing:** Vitest, Testing Library, jsdom\n\n**Build Tools:**\n- Vite 7.3.1 for fast development\n- TypeScript 5.9.3\n- Path aliases configured (@components, @lib, @hooks, etc.)\n\n---\n\n### 7. Integration Patterns\n\n**State Flow:**\n```\nGame.tsx (Controller)\n  ├── Manages all state (grid, flux, score, phase, settings, levels)\n  ├── Coordinates libraries (simulation, movement, scoring, level)\n  ├── Passes state to UI components\n  └── Handles callbacks from UI components\n```\n\n**Component Integration:**\n- Parent components pass callbacks down\n- No prop drilling beyond 1-2 levels\n- Custom hooks encapsulate complex logic\n- Libraries are pure functions with no side effects\n\n**Audio Integration:**\n- SoundEngine instance created once in Game.tsx\n- Audio callbacks passed down to components\n- Sounds triggered on interactions and state changes\n\n**Data Persistence:**\n- localStorage for expert settings\n- localStorage for per-level high scores\n- No global state manager - each component manages its slice\n\n---\n\n### Summary\n\nThis is a **high-quality, complete implementation** of Conway's Game of Life transformed into an engaging puzzle game. The codebase demonstrates:\n\n- **Professional architecture** with clean separation of concerns\n- **Comprehensive feature set** including pattern recognition, scoring, progression\n- **Excellent code quality** with TypeScript, testing, and linting\n- **Polished UX** with animations, audio, and responsive design\n- **Extensive configurability** through expert settings panel\n- **Production-ready** with no incomplete features or TODOs\n\nThe only minor issues are missing CSS files for `VictoryScreen` and `TransitionOverlay`, but these components use inline styles or minimal styling, so it's not a functional blocker.\n</task_result>","title":"Study source code structure","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b55b817ffe4xO5Z72BOIqlsR","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771215407276,"end":1771215521169}}}}
