r settings access, only expert shortcuts  \n**Spec**: expert-settings.md requires \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" menu path  \n**Action Needed**: Implement a proper settings menu/hamburger button for non-expert users\n\n### 3. High Score Persistence (Sprint 2.5 - [ ] Not Confirmed)\n**Status**: Implemented in level.ts but unclear if fully integrated with UI  \n**Impact**: Players can't see or track their high scores during gameplay  \n**Spec**: scoring-system.md requires high score display and persistence  \n**Action Needed**: Verify high scores are displayed during gameplay (not just at end of level)\n\n---\n\n## **HIGH PRIORITY** (Enhanced Features)\n\n### 4. Presets System (Sprint 5.2 - [ ] Entire Sprint Not Implemented)\n**Status**: No preset functionality exists  \n**Spec**: expert-settings.md mentions \"Easy, Normal, Hard, Chaos\" presets  \n**Impact**: No quick way for users to balance gameplay  \n**Action Needed**: \n- Implement preset dropdown in SettingsPanel\n- Create preset configuration objects (Easy: generous resources, Normal: balanced, Hard: strict, Chaos: extreme)\n- Add preset selection UI\n\n### 5. Expert Settings Validation UI (Sprint 5.1 - Partially [ ])\n**Status**: Settings panel exists but missing some validation and danger zone  \n**Spec**: expert-settings.md requires:\n- Schema validation with Zod or similar [ ]\n- \"Danger Zone\" section for extreme settings [ ]\n- Tooltips/documentation for each parameter [ ]\n- Visual indicator when value differs from default [ ]  \n**Action Needed**: Add comprehensive validation, danger zone, tooltips, and default value indicators\n\n### 6. Cell Animation Verification (Sprint 4.2 - Status unclear)\n**Status**: Implementation found in CanvasGrid.tsx and GridInteraction.tsx (birth/death animations)  \n**Plan**: Marked as [ ] but appears implemented  \n**Action Needed**: Verify animations are working correctly and remove [ ] if complete\n\n---\n\n## **MEDIUM PRIORITY** (Polish & UX)\n\n### 7. Touch Ripple Effect (Sprint 4.3 - [ ] Optional Not Implemented)\n**Status**: Not implemented  \n**Spec**: Mobile ripple animation for touch feedback  \n**Impact**: Minor - mobile UX enhancement  \n**Action Needed**: Add CSS/JS ripple effect on button touches\n\n### 8. Error Boundary (Sprint 6.1 - [ ] Not Implemented)\n**Status**: No React error boundary component  \n**Spec**: Catch React component errors, display user-friendly error message  \n**Impact**: Stability - app crashes show white screen  \n**Action Needed**: Create ErrorBoundary component and wrap App\n\n### 9. Input Validation (Sprint 6.1 - [ ] Not Implemented)\n**Status**: Some validation exists, but comprehensive validation missing  \n**Spec**: Validate all user inputs, prevent NaN/infinity  \n**Impact**: Edge cases could cause crashes  \n**Action Needed**: Add comprehensive input validation throughout\n\n---\n\n## **LOW PRIORITY** (Quality of Life)\n\n### 10. Accessibility Features (Sprint 6.2 - [ ] Mostly Not Implemented)\n**Status**: Only one ARIA label found (UIToggleButton.tsx)  \n**Spec**: Requires keyboard navigation, screen reader support, reduced motion, high contrast mode  \n**Impact**: Accessibility compliance  \n**Action Needed**: \n- Full keyboard navigation (arrow keys, tab order)\n- Screen reader announcements\n- prefers-reduced-motion support\n- High contrast toggle\n\n### 11. Performance Monitoring (Sprint 6.3 - [ ] Not Implemented)\n**Status**: No FPS counter or profiling tools  \n**Impact**: Development and optimization  \n**Action Needed**: Add FPS counter (dev mode only), memory tracking\n\n### 12. Documentation (Sprint 6.5 - [ ] Not Implemented)\n**Status**: No README.md file found in project root  \n**Impact**: Developer onboarding and user documentation  \n**Action Needed**: \n- Write README.md with installation, controls, configuration\n- Document API interfaces\n- Create developer guide\n\n---\n\n## **ALREADY IMPLEMENTED** (Remove [ ] from plan)\n\n### Cell Animations (Sprint 1.9 / 4.2)\n- Birth animations: Fade-in (0.1s) with scale effect ✅\n- Death animations: Shrink (0.15s) with fade ✅  \n- Invalid action flash (0.2s) ✅\n\n### Flux Counter Animations (Sprint 4.2)\n- Smooth 300ms value transitions ✅\n- Color coding (green → yellow → orange → red) ✅\n\n### Mobile Triple-Tap Gesture (Sprint 4.3 / 5.1)\n- useTripleTapGesture hook implemented ✅\n- Integrated with Game.tsx ✅\n\n### Audio Sonification (Sprint 4.1)\n- All sounds implemented (generation, interaction, transitions) ✅\n- SoundEngine class complete ✅\n\n---\n\n## **TEST STATUS**\n- **349 tests passing** ✅\n- Some test warnings (act() wrapper, AudioContext mock) but non-critical\n- Tests cover most implemented features\n\n---\n\n## **SUMMARY**\n\n**Most Critical Missing Features** (Top 3):\n1. **Pattern Breakdown UI** - Shows real-time scoring breakdown (already coded, just not displayed)\n2. **Settings Menu UI** - Non-expert users need a visible menu path\n3. **Presets System** - Quick gameplay balance options for different skill levels\n\n**Quick Wins** (Can be done in minutes):\n- Enable pattern breakdown UI by setting `showPatternBreakdown={true}`\n- Add simple settings menu button\n- Add high score display during gameplay\n\n**Large Effort Items**:\n- Full accessibility implementation\n- Comprehensive error handling\n- Performance optimization suite\n- Documentation\n\nThe codebase is very well-structured with most core features fully implemented and tested. The gaps are primarily in polish, UX enhancements, and optional features rather than core functionality.\n</task_result>","title":"Find unimplemented items","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39b55b7ffffeXnNHFEuEr81g3O","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771215407278,"end":1771215535144}}}}
